course: dictionary
lesson: 9384
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. Spout is one of these words. Read the whole sentence before you decide what it means.
explain: «Steam came out of the spout of the kettle.» Here the spout is the short tube you pour from. «The whale blew a tall spout into the cold air.» Here the spout is a strong stream of water and air, not a tube at all.
explain: Spout can also be a verb, meaning to send out liquid in a strong stream. Informally, it can mean talking a lot about silly things: «He spouts nonsense all day.» Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A spout is a short tube or lip on a teapot, kettle or jug that liquid is poured out of.
fact: A spout can also be a strong stream of liquid, such as a whale's spout of water and air.
fact: To spout means to come or send out liquid in a strong stream, as in «The fountain spouts water».
fact: Informally, to spout means to talk a lot, often saying silly or boring things.
fact: «Up the spout» (UK, informal) means ruined or wasted.
exercise: «Steam rose from the spout of the kettle.» What is the spout here? | The handle you hold the kettle by | *The short tube the liquid pours out of | The button you press to switch it on | The lid that keeps the heat in
exercise: «A whale blew a tall spout into the cold sea air.» What does spout mean here? | A fish with fins | *A strong stream of water and air | A kind of small wooden boat | A shy, quiet noise
exercise: «He spouts nonsense all day.» What does spouts mean? | Sings a happy song | Runs fast like a greyhound | Cleans the floor very quickly | *Talks a lot, saying silly things
test: «The fountain spouted water high into the air.» What does spouted mean? | Dried up slowly in the sun | *Sent out liquid in a strong stream | Froze solid in the cold | Made a soft sound like a whisper
test: «Our picnic went up the spout when the rain came.» What does up the spout mean? | Hidden under the table | *Ruined or wasted | Made very tall | Carried up a tall hill
exam: «Dad spouts about football all evening, and nobody listens.» What does spouts mean here? | Pours out of a jug | Sends out a strong stream of water | Kicks the ball very hard | *Talks a lot, often about boring things
